ore of the god of  mischief via some flashback scenes to a  young Loki antagonizing his brother Thor  the tone that Taika Waititi wanted for  those flashbacks were similar to the  classic 80s films of writer director  John Hughes such as sixteen Candles one  of the flashbacks would have popped up  during the scene on Sokka where Loki is  tied up in Valkyrie banner and Thora all  talking about how he wants to kill them  which leads Thor to recount the time  when he and Loki were eight years old  and Loki transformed himself into a  snake before quickly transforming back  and stabbing Thor a flashback here could  have been a fun moment but according to  ITT in the end it was one thing too many  to add to the movie and the story was  funnier the way Chris Hemsworth told it  ytt also revealed to MTV that another  John Hughes inspired scene ended up cut  from the movie the idea was that when  Thor and Balki met in the film they  realized they already knew each other  then there was going to be a flashback  to 1980s Asgard where everyone had  mullets and wore his shoulder pads in  the cutscene Thor was going to be an  overweight child who was being picked on  by  the kids and Loki would have been an emo  goth character a bit like Draco Malfoy  from Harry Potter the problem with this  scene was that in the final story they  needed Thor not to have met Valkyrie  before so the flashback wouldn't have  worked there's also a deleted promo  scene between Doctor Strange and Thor at  strangers sanctum sanctorum destiny has  dire plans for you my friend  I have dire plans for destiny I wonder  if this deleted scene suggests that  Doctor Strange has some foreknowledge of  the events of Ragnarok that are about to  be unleashed there's also a nice Star  Wars esque shot and line that was teased  in the trailer but ended up cut from the  movie as well in an interview with  Rolling Stone Tessa Thompson who plays  Valkyrie revealed that his scene  alluding to her character's bisexuality  was cut from the final film Thompson  said that after researching her  character in the comics she learned  about Valkyries relationship with  archaeologist Annabelle Riggs so she  convinced ytt to film a scene of a woman  leaving her bedroom implying the two had  been intimate however according to the  interview the moment was deleted because  it took focus away from the main  narrative at the time but with Valkyrie  back for a small role and Avengers  infinity war and thompson having  recently pitched an all-female team up  movie to marvel Valkyrie sexuality could  be something that's addressed in a  future movie and talking a female  Asgardian warriors one fan favorite  missing from the third movie is Lady SIF  Jamie Alexander recently confirmed that  she was indeed asked to return to the  role but scheduling conflicts with her  TV series blind spots meant she couldn't  make it  the curious thing though is back in 2015  Jamie Alexander said she would  definitely be back for the latest Thor  film and that she would have a pivotal  role this makes me wonder whether at  that time Valkyrie wasn't supposed to  feature in the movie or at least not as  heavily and whether the original plan  was perceived to play a part similar to  that instead I guess Alexander's lead in  blind spot the first two seasons of  which are over 20 episodes meant it was  too hard to give SIF a major role in the  new film but at least sifts absence  means she wasn't killed off by Heller  has happened to the Warriors three  so SIF could still reappear in the MCU  which Alexander says she'll be very  happy to do this array bill is a popular  character from the comics and although  an Easter Egg to him virus statue  outside the Grand Master's palace he  never actually appears in the movie  according to Kevin Feige though at one  point beater a bill was going to be in  the film however they felt they weren't  doing his character justice so they  can't his appearance altogether and just  left the easter egg though they may well  introduce him in a later movie Heller  was one of the highlights of Thor  Ragnarok thanks to an interesting  backstory great Swagger and an actress  to match she's also the first female  lead villain in an MCU movie however  Taika Waititi revealed that another  Marvel Comics villain called paratus was  originally going to be in the film ytt  didn't elaborate on whether the  character would have been instead of  heller  however it's interesting that paratus  who's a much more obscure villain shares  some similar comic-book history to  Heller's arc in Thor Ragnarok in the  comics paratus is a dark God who's  defeated by Odin when he and the other  dark gods attack as God to punish para  cos Odin imprisons him in a special cell  in a distant part of the universe that  only the all-father has access to in a  similar way to how he keeps heller  locked away in the MCU also like Heller  paratus destroyed Thor's hammer when he  chomped it in half in the comics some of  the parallels between the two characters  are close enough that I wonder how much  para cos provided inspiration for  Heller's backstory in the movie I'm  still glad that Heller was a final  choice though if she gave us one of the  better MCU villains so far and I'm also  really glad she didn't end up being the  villain in Thor the dark world as was  originally going to be the case  another Ragnarok highlight is Jeff  Goldblum's take on the Grand Master with  the veteran actor bringing some great  off-the-wall humor to his eccentric  Sekar and dictator however if you look  at the comic book version of his  character you'll notice he has blue skin  according to Taika Waititi the reason  for the change in the movie was that  Goldblum already played the part of a  blue alien in the 1988 sci-fi musical  comedy earth girls are easy still  Ragnarok does include some little  allusions to the grandmasters original  comic book look with blue eyeliner and a  little blue strip on his face which is  also a nod to the fact he's related to  the MC news collector set visits for  Thor Ragnarok also reported seeing  concept art of a meeting between the  Grand Master and guardians of the galaxy  character the broker in the first  guardians movie the broker planned to  buy the orb which contained the power  stone for the  lector / film also reported that an item  courtesan durian cube was found on the  propolis in the movies production office  and that concept art of the Guardians  Milano ship was found on set as well  none of these Guardians connections  ended up in the movie and I wonder if  they were possibly infinity stone  related in some way cookie of Infinity  stones Marvel fans waiting for the final  reveal of the soul stone and thor  ragnarok were disappointed there were  hints and theories that seeing Halla  bathed in orange light after destroying  Thor's hammer and the trailers indicated  she'd acquired the soul stone for Mele  near but with that scenery shot and  relocated it's possible though not  especially likely that Marvel midway  through production decided to remove any  soul stone connection in the movie there  is however speculation the soul stone  was in the eternal flame which brought  Serta back to life at the end of the  film and that this could tie in with  Alice's arrival at the very end in the  mid credits and on the subjective and  credit scenes Jeff Goldblum told Digital  Spy that thanks to Taika Waititi strong  preference for improvisation on set they  filmed around 20 different versions of  his post-credits scene some of them  include the Grandmaster trying to start  a new revolution to overthrow the  current revolution and in another he  starts singing the Saqqara national  anthem speaking to Fandango ytt also  said there was an extended version of  the melt stick scene featuring the  Grandmaster speaking at length to his  cousin Carlo before he zaps him and in  the scenes at the arena there were much  lengthier versions of the Grand Master's  speeches to the crowd during which  Goldblum riffed on all kinds of subjects  at my titi threw at him including  licensing a car plus is a deleted scene  involving mine between the Grand Master  and topaz after he sends Loki and Bal  curry off to find Thor and the Hulk  whitey T's emphasis on improvised comedy  and thor ragnarok means we can probably  expect a lot of unused comedic gem some  of which will hopefully appear on the  blu-ray and DVD now what do you think  about any of the deleted scenes or  things which didn't make it into thor  ragnarok is there anything you wish had  been included or are you happy with the  final movie let me know your thoughts in  the comments below and don't forget to  subscribe for your chance to win a  marvel Funko pop or and obsessed with  Marvel book I'll announce the winners on  my upcoming Justice League videos so  turn on your notifications to get those  as soon as I post them if you enjoyed  this then do hit that like  button and check out more of my marvel  and deleted scenes videos right here  thanks for watching and see you next  time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers
 

